// onsa.toml
// [test]
// mode = "none"
// spec = ["§2.4", "§2.5"]

// Interpolation holes that hold multi-byte characters (R-01, S-90): right after the `{`, after a
// `.`, inside a path, next to the escapes `{{` `}}`, and characters that §2.5 does not allow
// (controls, line separators, bidirectional controls) or that are not identifier characters
// (BOM, NBSP, emoji, full-width forms, combining marks). Each line is a string the lexer has to
// walk character by character; the file has to round-trip (the diagnostics are in
// tests/spec/negative/lex_utf8_holes.onsa). The last line has an open hole at the end of the file.

